{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head a427d61171c56f4a16a4fa29188162f3aa7381c5. It changes documents and notes and no source path, so no gate is owed. Every number matches the planner's evidence, and each of your five points holds. Two small items are for a later edit.\n\n**The numbers.** I read `call2.json` and `call2b.json` in the planner's evidence (`SHA256SUMS` b56d230d, every digest verifies). They give the control at 209.0 s, the 60-second case at 208.9 s, and the revoked case at 209.4 s with `atSeconds` 31.2. `bytesThrough` is 4,579,898 at the revocation and 31,558,649 at the end, `lsRemoteExit` is 128, and `headMatches` is true in all three. So 178 s and 27 MB are right, and both are labelled as arithmetic. \"Twice\" is right for revoking by ID: call 1 once, and call 2 once in `call2b`.\n\n**1. The 149 seconds: correct, and it errs low.** The token was minted before the clone began, so its end came at or before 60 s into the clone. The real gap is at least 148.9 s. \"About 149, by arithmetic from the lifetime that the planner asked for\" is honest.\n\n**2. The difference from 908b6d86: right.** The run shows a 60-second token ending during a clone. The 3600-second tokens never reached their end. \"No clone ran past a one-hour token\" states what ran. The act's sentence reaches further than that, and the note keeps the risk open without contradicting the planner's ruling on the pin.\n\n**3. The `dap log destination` row: correct by reading, with one sentence owed at a later edit.** `entryLine` (`commands.ts:694`) prints `delivery tell from directory:\u003cseq\u003e`, and `scopeNamed` accepts `destination` (`:166`). I ran a read-only script over destination @1 to @17, and `compromised` is the only `tell` from a directory on every pin. So the row identifies a notice. The row prints the same for a notice that the guard refused, and the page does not say that. The guard refuses only a sender other than this room's directory, and platform directories send only to their own destination, so I do not expect such a row in practice. The operator's order also does not rest on this row, because the steps keep the wait. So this does not hold the head. At the next edit, please add that the row shows neither which key the notice names nor whether the destination applied it. `dap log` also shows the last 20 entries by default, so a person on a busy destination needs `--limit`.\n\n**4. Mara's sentence: right.** \"Only commits that no download reached\" counts what a download goes on to reach after the revocation, and the act's words undercount that. The table row and the sentence beside it agree with it. The scene keeps its limit: \"one run at 30 MB\".\n\n**5. The heading, the opening and the status: correct.** They match 908b6d86 and 9af818a5. The older \"real calls 2 and 3\" phrase survives only in the status line, as the history of the ruling in cccd205a, with the later ruling beside it. I searched the docs and the note for the old claims \"safe from\", \"fails every time\" and \"cuts a reply\", and each remaining line carries the new limit. The sentence \"the note's cost did not appear at this size\" stays limited to Artifacts and 30 MB.\n\n**The stolen-key section.** \"A new request with the token\" now bounds the 24 hours and 600 seconds, and the unrun cases are listed. No statement there says more than the run shows, and the buffer is named as unmeasured. The token-refusal note's `sealedDelivery` sentence is now marked as read and not run, which is the next-edit item from 35d1ea10.\n\n**The manifest's `directory`.** `docs/testing.md:706` asks for the absolute directory path. Each of the last five manifests holds a relative name, and check-notes accepts that. The relative name is the better form, because it holds no home path. So the document is the thing to change, at any later edit, and this head need not differ from its neighbours.\n\n**Evidence.** The new unit's `SHA256SUMS` is 90d37918…, every digest verifies, and no file is writable. The head after checkpoint e90c2b37 changes only the note and its manifest. I reran check-notes (0 warnings), check-doc-links (801, 0 broken), check-commit-messages (4, 0 flagged), and confirmed that no source path changed. The worktree is clean. I ran no test. I did not read Cloudflare's pages.\n\n**Architecture.** No source, pin or contract changes. The design note now separates a new request from a download under way, which is the distinction that the run showed.\n\n**Security.** This head corrects a statement that said more than a revocation does. It weakens no statement, and an operator now treats a clone under way as having what it reached.\n\n**Simplification.** Nothing to remove.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4074b265ef7546d300fae5cdccea48895192125f","binding":"assigned","head":"a427d61171c56f4a16a4fa29188162f3aa7381c5","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8ad1bdeb724a03d16a790ae66281fab1474955a3\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:50498032d6381a42e01c97fcb1c13cae73104881\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1efebcc0c6b4ca6c4026ae219f28eb70a6fd072c","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}